{"abstract":"This paper examines the generality of features extracted from heart rate (HR) and skin conductance (SC) signals as predictors of self-reported player affect expressed as pairwise preferences. Artificial neural networks are trained to accurately map physiological features to expressed affect in two dissimilar and independent game surveys. The performance of the obtained affective models which are trained on one game is tested on the unseen physiological and self- reported data of the other game. Results in this early study suggest that there exist features of HR and SC such as average HR and one and two-step SC variation that are able to predict affective states across games of different genre and dissimilar game mechanics.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Martínez, Héctor Pérez","Garbarino, Maurizio","Yannakakis, Georgios N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382159"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Polytechnic University of Milan"],"keyword":["Cross game prediction","Heart rate variability","Physiological signals","Player affect","Skin conductance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"generic physiological features as predictors of player experience","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/80054838228","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382159","identifier":[{"id":"80054838228","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3ca82dae-04fb-4f4c-9c4a-e2ed2cd2745d"],"keyword":["Cross-game prediction","Heart rate variability","Physiological signals","Player affect","Skin conductance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-18CEF9BF0B312233ABC07EEAD1F9E16C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"polytechnic university of milan","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnic University of Milan","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Héctor Pérez","key":"martínezpau","last":"Martínez","name":"Martínez, Héctor Pérez","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maurizio","key":"garbarinopau","last":"Garbarino","name":"Garbarino, Maurizio","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Georgios N.","key":"yannakakispau","last":"Yannakakis","name":"Yannakakis, Georgios N.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9783642245992"],"pages":"267-276","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"ACII'11 Proceedings of the 4th international conference on Affective computing and intelligent interaction","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80054838228"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3ca82dae-04fb-4f4c-9c4a-e2ed2cd2745d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Generic Physiological Features as Predictors of Player Experience","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382159","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
